 \r\r Carl Herman, Conejo-Las Virgenes Future Foundation, provided an update on the Future Foundation�s current activities and its plan for the future. Mary Hath Spokane, spoke regarding global warming\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r\r Approval of the minutes for the September 13, 2006 City Council meeting. \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1045, amending Resolution No. 2004-915 and re-adopting the City�s Conflict of Interest Code.\r\r Adoption of Resolution Nos. 2006-1046, 2006-1047, 2006-1048, and 2006-1049, for the Calabasas General Municipal Election to be held March 6, 2007.\r\r Recommendation to approve a Professional Services Agreement with Rehab Financial Corporation in the amount of $173,800 to perform professional CDBG administrative services.\r\r Recommendation to approve renewal contract with A2B Transportation for transit services.\r\r Adoption of Ordinance No. 2006-228, amending Chapter 1.16 of Title 1 and Chapter 8.2 of Title 8 of the Calabasas Municipal Code regarding the abatement of nuisances and the recovery of abatement costs. \r\r Recommendation from the Parks, Recreation and Education Commission to approve a grant request from Save Open Space submitted as part of the first funding cycle of FY 06/07.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1050, directing staff to proceed with the implementation of the General Plan update workplan and establishing a General Plan Advisory Committee (GPAC) to guide the General Plan update process.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1051, approving an Addendum to the Certified Final EIR and Adopted Mitigated Declarations for the City of Calabasas Civic Center Project.\r\rCouncilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to approve Item #1, 3, 4, 5, 6, and 9 with revision to language in Addendum in Item #9 to correct a typographical error. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Mayor Washburn was absent.\r\r Following discussion, Councilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to continue Item #2. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Mayor Washburn was absent.\r\rFollowing discussion, Councilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to not approve #7 and to reject the Parks, Recreation and Education Commission�s recommendation to approve a grant request from Save Open Space. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Mayor Washburn was absent.\r\rFollowing discussion, Councilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson to approve #8. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Mayor Washburn was absent.\r\r\r\rPUBLIC HEARING \r\r CONTINUED PUBLIC HEARING � Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1014, establishing revised affordable housing in-lieu fees for residential development projects and a revised affordable housing impact fee for commercial development projects, in accordance with Chapter 17.22 of the Municipal Code. \r\rThe Item was continued to October 18, 2006.\r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS \r\r Update on Zip Code Change and Postal Service Issues.\r\rJohn Bingham, Senior Management Analyst, presented the staff report.\r\rNo Action Taken.\r\rNEW BUSINESS \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1025, approving the Calabasas Creek Master Plan for restoration.\r\rAlex Farassati, Environmental Services Manager, presented the staff report.\r\rCouncilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to adopt Resolution No. 2006-1025, approving the Calabasas Creek Master Plan. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Mayor Washburn was absent.\r\r Contribution of $200,000 towards the MRCA acquisition of Lincoln Properties/Caplan APN 2069-010-017.\r\rMaureen Tamuri, Community Development Director, presented the staff report.\r\rMary Hubbard, Calabasas, spoke in support of the acquisition of the property.\r\rCouncilmember Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to approve the contribution of $200,000 towards the MRCA acquisition. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Mayor Washburn was absent.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r Receive and file the Fiscal Year 2005-2006 Community Development Department Annual Report.\r\rGeoff Starns, Senior Planner, presented the staff report.\r\rNo Action Taken.\r\r Check Register for the period of September 1, 2006 to September 14, 2006.\r\rNo Action Taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\r Councilmember Wolfson announced that the bid opening for the Civic Center Project Bid has been extended to October 10, 2006.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT\r\r City Manager Coroalles stated that there was nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\r\r Councilmember Wolfson requested that an update on the Spirit of Calabasas senior center rebuilding project in Plaquemines Parish be placed on a future agenda.\r\rADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 9:15 p.m.\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 4 -\u0015\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u